title: A Putsch is being launched by Kapp-Lüttwitz!
subtitle: The forces of reaction rear their heads again.
view-if: kapp_putsch_seen = 0 and year = 1920 and month = 3
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: kapp_putsch_seen = 1; month_actions += 1
tags: event
new-page: true

= Kapp-Lüttwitz Putsch!

<img src="img/kapp_luttwitz.jpeg" style="float:left; margin-right:1em; margin-bottom:0.5em; width:320px; object-fit:cover; object-position:top; border:4px solid #000000ff;"> The <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">**Rep**</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**ub**</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">**lic**</span> is in crisis! Several units of the Freikorps, <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Marinebrigades Ehrhardt</span> and <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Loewenfeld</span>, have defied orders from Reichswehr Minister Noske to disband during the SPD’s steady winding down of the Freikorps and other paramilitary forces following the Revolution. General Lüttwitz and several other sympathetic forces, including large swathes of the bureaucracy, have joined them.

Already, the disloyal Freikorps are in Berlin, and more are going to follow - a <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Putschist</span> government is expected to form, and the Reichswehr is starting to defect.... If we do not stop them, all we have fought for will be gone and reaction will have won, forever, destroying our new <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">**Rep**</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**ub**</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">**lic**</span>..

What should we do?

- @general_strike: We must support the <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">**Rep**</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**ub**</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">**lic**</span> and general strike to bring down this illegitimate government!
- @statement: Send out a statement that we support the <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">**Rep**</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**ub**</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">**lic**</span> but stay neutral on the general strike.
- @negotiate: Officially negotiate with the Kapp government?

@general_strike
subtitle: Down with the reactionaries!
on-arrival: linksliberale_strength += 10; nationalliberale_dissent += 10; old_middle_ddp -= 6*(1-dissent); workers_ddp += 8*(1-dissent); spd_relation += 12; dvp_relation -= 8; dnvp_relation -= 10; ddp_industrial_backing -= 2; z_relation += 12; uspd_relation += 4

<img src="img/general_strike.jpeg" style="float:left; margin-right:1em; margin-bottom:0.5em; width:220px; object-fit:cover; object-position:top; border:4px solid #000000ff;"> We have officially condemned the <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Putsch</span> as the party is fully united against <span style="color: var(--nsdap-colour);">undemocratic</span> coup, on the following day of the <span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">socialist</span> general strike the party published a full article on the denouncing the putschists as traitors of the <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">**Ge**</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**rm**</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">**an**</span> state, and defended the general strike of the free unions as "a concerted protest of the <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">**Ge**</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**rm**</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">**an**</span> nation against the frivolous attempt to overthrow the constitution and system of law to which hundreds of thousands of German civil servants has sworn loyalty to". Our own members have fled Berlin with the exception of Eugen Schiffer who has voluntarily remained to negotiate with the <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Kapp</span> government to stall for time.

As for the <span style="color: var(--nlp-colour);">National Liberal</span> DVP, they have attributed the cause of the coup as the inability of the incubent government to call for new elections after the new constitution and displayed open sympathy to the <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Putsch</span>. They also denounced the general strike as an invitation to civil war and that it needs to be stopped as the precondition to restore law and order. However as the collapse of the <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Putsch</span> becomes more apparant, they have switched their tone to support the constitution while calling for snap election to end the National Assembly that is dominated by the <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">We</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">im</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">ar</span> Coalition. We have criticized the <span style="color: var(--dvp-colour);">People's Party</span> for their opportunism however our ability to capitalize on the situation is being hampered significantly due to our endorsement of the general strike, as our middle class voters have not taken this kindly. Now we have another problem- the <span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">socialist</span> general strike hasnt ended after <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Kapp</span> resigned and they are likely to make demands soon..

@statement
subtitle: The SPD and Z might not be that happy.
on-arrival: workers_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); rural_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); catholics_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); sammlung_dissent += 3; linksliberale_dissent += 3; nationalliberale_dissent += 3; pazifisten_dissent += 3 

<img src="img/ddp_poster_32.webp" style="float:left; margin-right:1em; margin-bottom:0.5em; width:220px; object-fit:cover; object-position:top; border:4px solid #000000ff;"> We have officially condemned the <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">Putsch</span> as the party is fully united against <span style="color: var(--nsdap-colour);">undemocratic</span> coup, on the following day of the socialist general strike the party published a full article on the denouncing the putschists as traitors of the German state, and however we have purposely avoided to send out a clear stance regarding the socialist general strike to not further alienate our middle class voters, annoying part of our left liberals. As for the National Liberal DVP, they have attributed the cause of the coup as the inability of the incubent government to call for new elections after the new constitution and displayed open sympathy to the Putsch. They also denounced the general strike as an invitation to civil war and that it needs to be stopped as the precondition to restore law and order. However as the collapse of the Putsch becomes more apparant, they have switched their tone to support the constitution while calling for snap election to end the National Assembly that is dominated by the Weimar coalition.

We have criticized the People's party for their opportunism and we are able to capitalize greatly on the situation with the DVP unable to muster up a rebuttal to our criticism. But now we have another problem- the socialist general strike, that we have to negotiate with. May their demands be reasonable or else it will be another crisis.

@negotiate
unavailable-subtitle: We are a <span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">democratic</span> party and we will never negotiate with these militant <span style="color: var(--nsdap-colour);">extremists</span>!
choose-if: false
